# liquifai: shell-completion behaviour; none is needed to run an app (docs/shell-completion.md)

# LIQUIFAI_NO_LAZY_COMPLETE=   1 stops a TAB from starting a background refresh of the completion caches
# LIQUIFAI_BG_REFRESH=   1 refreshes stale value caches in the background after every successful command
# LIQUIFAI_COMPLETION_LIST=grouped   grouped | plain — the second TAB's listing: grouped with help, or the shell's sorted list (docs/shell-completion.md)
# LIQUIFAI_COMPLETION_COLOR=auto   auto | always | never — the grouped listing in colour; auto: unless NO_COLOR is set or the terminal is dumb (docs/shell-completion.md)
# NO_COLOR=   any value turns the colour of the grouped listing off under LIQUIFAI_COMPLETION_COLOR=auto (no-color.org)

# not for .env: LIQUIFAI_COMPLETE_WIRE LIQUIFAI_COMPLETE_SHELL — set by the generated completion script: its reply format, and zsh naming itself
# not for .env: COMP_LINE COMP_POINT COMP_TYPE COMP_WORDS COMP_CWORD — set by the shell while it completes
# not for .env: XDG_CACHE_HOME — set by the desktop session; where the completion caches live
